WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:02.700
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.820
So this is gonna to be my 'Flash Episode 13' video.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.480
All about Firestorm.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.360
The title of the episode was "Nuclear Man".

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:13.618
So this was the introduction of what Firestorm is gonna look like in the DCTV Universe.

00:00:13.618 --> 00:00:19.238
Just like with Barry Allen's Flash suit, the producers have said that there will be an evolution of the Firestorm costume.

00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:22.838
So, the costume that we saw in this episode will change over time.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.880
They've taken their time introducing the character, but I think, once they establish him, they'll start using him more often.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.160
What I'd really like to see is Firestorm become a critical part of the finale.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.740
I'll try to dig through that a little bit as I work through my Top 5 Moments and the Easter Eggs.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.723
There's a whole bunch of stuff going on in the episode so I'll explain some of the really big stuff first.

00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:42.638
Okay, just careful for spoilers from the episode if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:43.378
So let's get going.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.980
Starting with 'Blood Samples':

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.660
Cisco said that one was Barry's from the future 

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.180
(so we're talking like, older Barry Allen that goes back in time) 

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.037
...and the other one was, "unknown".

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.338
Meaning, it was not a match for Wells.

00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:58.620
A lot of you were asking questions about this on Twitter while the episode was going on.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:00:59.320
So.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.600
He said that he tested both samples. 

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.240
Meaning that he tested Wells' sample, and it was not a match.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.040
Meaning, there are two Reverse Flashes.

00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:08.541
I don't really consider that news. 

00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:10.181
I always felt like there were gonna be two Flashes.

00:01:10.181 --> 00:01:12.041
There's gonna be a CRAZY Reverse Flash

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.360
and there'll be the 'Harrison Wells' Reverse Flash (that's trying to save his wife).

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.460
Here's what I think the producers are doing with the two villain characters (the two Reverse Flashes):

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.480
They're just mixing and matching aspects of ALL the Reverse Flashes.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.580
So it'd be kinda misleading to call one of them Hunter Zolomon, and one of them Professor Zoom.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:32.260
Because you'll have like an 'Eobard Thawne' character, with aspects of Hunter Zolomon's character.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.980
So whenever they finally reveal everything, what we'll say is like,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.080
"This is Eobard Thawne, with Hunter Zolomon's backstory"

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.478
Or, "This is Hunter Zolomon, with some aspects from Eobard Thawne's history"

00:01:42.478 --> 00:01:44.598
So just remember that when you're theory-crafting.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.680
And yes, I think it was the 'Crazy' Reverse Flash that killed Barry's mother.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.380
As much as Harrison Wells seemed like a dick in this episode -- 

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.780
like he wanted to kill Ronnie Raymond and Prof. Martin Stein to stop the nuclear reaction

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.920
 -- he shared his fries, AND he sacrificed the Tachyon Prototype. 

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.431
He cannibalized that to make the Firestorm Device.

00:02:00.431 --> 00:02:05.391
Technically you could call him a villain, because he is the Reverse Flash, and he's deceiving everyone.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.500
He hurt a lot of people for selfish reasons.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.880
But that doesn't mean that he's a psychotic serial killer.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.840
And it seems like the other Reverse Flash (the one who's identity we don't know yet), it seems like he's more psychotic.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.080
I think once they introduce time travel on the show in the next couple of episodes, 

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.540
we'll start to learn WHO that other Reverse Flash is.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.680
And also, if you were confused by why they lingered on the shot of that Flash Ring 

00:02:24.684 --> 00:02:28.824
(while Harrison Wells was, you know, holding his neck with the Flash ring really clear in-frame)

00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:32.164
I think what they're teasing with that is that he just has a much deeper connection to the Flash.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.700
A lot of people, when we first met him, thought he might be a future-version of Barry Allen. 

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:36.880
Especially with the Flash Ring.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.520
But, the Reverse Flash also* gets a Flash Ring.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.160
Okay, so moving into the fun stuff.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:41.860
"Top 5 Moments"

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.980
No. 5: Driving safely while kissing a pretty girl.

00:02:44.986 --> 00:02:48.200
Probably one of the best Einstein quotes I've ever heard a TV show throw out.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.780
Victor Garber was saying it, talking about his life, but it shines a light on what's going on in Barry's life.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.820
It's what inspires him to go after her and eat that super hot pepper.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.240
That's the show telling us that they're going to continue to be a thing.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.340
I'm hoping Malese Jow stays on the show for a while.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.025
Because Linda Park is a really big part of the Flash history in the comics.

00:03:04.025 --> 00:03:05.460
...and Malese Jow is just a lot of fun.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.980
It's just nice to have a female on the show, with her energy.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.880
The show would be SO much less fun if no one was having sex on it.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.720
Actually, I felt like they really shined a light on that in this episode too.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.300
That there is a lot of sex happening in Central City.

00:03:17.306 --> 00:03:19.186
Especially in Barry's old house.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.600
'Cougar time for the win'

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.359
I'm gonna go ahead n'take a wild stab in the dark and say Joe, is not gonna tap that.

00:03:24.359 --> 00:03:30.680
The funny thing is, is that the actor that plays Cisco said that Cisco might be finding some romance himself at a certain point.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:37.880
Wouldn't it be funny if, in like a post-credits scene (or in the comic), you see him quietly go back to that house to go on a date with that woman?

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.080
That would be so gross and so funny at the same time.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:43.560
But I would* like to see them bring on, like, Brie Larson from Community. 

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.740
I feel like she would be a good date for Cisco.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.720
On to No. 4: Time Travel-Flash Cinema.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:55.140
Wasn't it awesome how they used the logic of the mirror to show, like, a projector reel of the Flashes fighting in the past?

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.680
We actually saw them digging a little bit deeper into that footage.

00:03:57.685 --> 00:03:59.845
They end up showing it to Barry in the next episode.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.271
So it's the show just pushing into the idea of time travel; they're going to start exploring time travel.

00:04:04.271 --> 00:04:06.620
That'll cross through the rest of the back of the season.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:11.020
So as we get further along in the episodes we'll eventually see Barry start to time travel.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:15.060
First it'll be kinda like the 'Groundhog Day' situation where he kinda stumbles through time travel;

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.480
he accidentally stumbles into it.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.100
I think by the end of the season he'll actually find a certain amount of control over time traveling.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.700
And, now that Harrison Wells has destroyed his Tachyon Device, he can't time travel.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.840
So if he's going to go back in time to save his wife, he's gonna have to find some other way to do it.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.800
Which actually leads in to some Firestorm stuff.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.640
So, onto No. 3: Firestorm ᵛˢ⋅ The Flash.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.840
This is before they get him under control.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.120
It's the big action-set-piece between the Flash and Firestorm.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.182
This was a lot of fun.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.400
It was really an FX sequence.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.580
And I feel like The Flash doesn't have a huge budget, but the FX always look great.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.720
There're usually ways to get around not having a lot of money for FX. 

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.940
One: you don't do them for an extended period of time.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.940
And Two: you try to shoot them at night so things don't stand out as much. 

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.720
So you don't focus as much on the details.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.800
That's also kinda how Arrow gets around their budget problems too.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.540
They both shoot 23 episodes a season, but they have a smaller budget than a lot of major network shows.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.640
So they don't have a lot of money to throw into FX.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.700
What I'm really interested to see is what Firestorm's powers look like 

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.700
now that he's slowly getting under control.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.580
Moving on to No. 2: 

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.540
Firestorm joins 'Team Flash'.

00:05:12.718 --> 00:05:14.418
So he's not officially on the team yet.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.100
What happened at the end of the episode (at least what it seemed like happened) is that they were successful

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.800
in separating Ronnie Raymond from Martin Stein.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.080
Their device worked.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.940
They have released some descriptions for some of the future episodes.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.000
They've teased that, obviously, I mean the Firestorm character's still going to be a thing on The Flash.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.080
But if they're going to BE Firestorm, they have to merge into The Matrix again.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:37.460
So they're prob'ly gonna use that device to become Firestorm again.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.760
I think mostly it's gonna be like a control device:

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.400
It'll help them control their powers.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.760
The real question is, 

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.400
Who's going to be controlling The Matrix?             Who's gonna be The Mind?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.340
And who'll be The Body?

00:05:46.538 --> 00:05:48.098
Obviously it's a really simple answer.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.440
I mean, Robbie Amell is gonna be the actor on the show. 

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:54.520
So it's always gonna be Martin Stein driving the car IN Ronnie Raymond's body (he'll be the car).

00:05:54.843 --> 00:05:57.980
They haven't said specifically whether or not they're doing it, but, what I'm hoping to see

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:02.660
is we get a shot of inside the Firestorm Matrix (with the 'floaty-heads' talking to each other).

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.260
It'd be kinda like being inside Tony Stark's helmet whenever he's talking to J.A.R.V.I.S. 

00:06:06.262 --> 00:06:10.862
Part of the energy, between Ronnie Raymond and Martin Stein in the comics, was the witty banter.

00:06:10.862 --> 00:06:12.362
So I'm really looking forward to that.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.840
And, my No. 1 Moment:

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.680
Alter Harrison Wells' plans, and General Eiling post-credits scene.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.935
It's a two-part episode so we've really only seen half the story.

00:06:20.935 --> 00:06:25.360
General Eiling is gonna try to capture Firestorm and use him for military purposes. 

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.580
As a weapon -- pretty likely.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.240
Like what he was gonna try and do with Plastique earlier this season.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.860
I also think that answers Jason Rush's comment from the previous episode. 

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.920
The "Mystery Backer" that they didn't know about (the person who provided the financial backing)?

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.740
...it was probably General Eiling.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.020
That's why I think that when they found out about the nuclear blast, he was like,

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:42.820
"BAM. Firestorm"

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.200
He didn't even need to think about it.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.540
He knew INSTANTLY what it was.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.440
So on the side of that:

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.720
Because Harrison Wells clearly does not like General Eiling, he'll prob'ly try to help them out.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.920
As part of Team Flash.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:59.080
But, as the Reverse Flash---in terms of his secret plans---he sacrificed the Tachyon Prototype to create the "Quantum Splicer".

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:04.260
I'm wondering if whatever new plan he comes up with to time travel, involves using Firestorm's energy.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:09.413
I think we should all remember, too, that the Reverse Flash is weak against Firestorm powers.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.660
Both hot and cold stuff.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.780
I mean that's why the Rogues are also very important; because they have those weapons.

00:07:13.789 --> 00:07:20.038
If Team Flash is gonna fight the Reverse Flash, I feel like it would benefit them to use Firestorm AND the Rogues.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.460
If they're gonna fight that villain they're gonna have to use weapons that he's weak against.

00:07:23.465 --> 00:07:25.925
And those other characters are the only ones that have those right now.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.840
It gets you even more pumped when Episode 18 is called,

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.960
"All-Star Team up"

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.620
Even though that doesn't refer to Firestorm.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:32.480
So let me know:

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.960
What was your favorite moment from the episode?

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.640
And where would you like to see them take the Firestorm character?

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.440
I mean, do you wanna see Captain Atom in S02 (because he's a big part of the Firestorm comics)?

00:07:41.442 --> 00:07:42.742
I think that would be awesome.

00:07:42.742 --> 00:07:47.660
Like, if they take their time introducing Firestorm, then they can introduce Captain Atom as part of that.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:48.680
All in all, great episode.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:52.240
So here are actually some of the Easter Eggs that I spotted that I haven't already mentioned yet:

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.120
One: "The Conway Award".

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.920
That's actually named after Jerry Conway.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.560
He's the person that created Firestorm in the comics.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:07:59.920
Barry Allen says,

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.340
"Please don't flame-on"

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:05.380
I know that sounds like a Fantastic Four reference, but that's ALSO a Firestorm reference.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.440
That's something he says in the comics whenever he fires his powers up.

00:08:08.445 --> 00:08:10.525
When they're talking about blood samples on the screen here: 

00:08:10.525 --> 00:08:13.040
They have both blue, and yellow samples.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.260
Visually, I just feel like this is an Easter Egg for the Reverse Flash -- the yellow blood sample.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:23.213
They also have a nice heads-up display for the Firestorm Matrix too (on these computer monitors while they're talking about it).

00:08:23.213 --> 00:08:25.260
We see Harrison Wells' Flash-ring here again.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:26.781
Very prominently displayed.

00:08:26.781 --> 00:08:29.523
I can't WAIT for Barry Allen to get a Flash-ring.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.280
In the comics it has a number of uses.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.960
Mostly the 'Wally West' Flash used it to contain his suit.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.277
So, when he was running around, the suit would come out of the ring.

00:08:38.277 --> 00:08:41.277
I feel like eventually we'll get there, but it might be a couple seasons away.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:42.200
And finally:

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.320
The 'adult' Blood Sample from Barry Allen

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.560
Very clearly, Barry Allen IS time traveling...right now...while The Flash is happening.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:53.240
An older version of Barry Allen is jumping around in the timestream, fighting the Reverse Flash.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:54.880
Trying to save his mother.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.439
Just like Harrison Wells, in the future, is probably trying to save his wife.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.300
Just to talk a little bit more about that too.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.140
Harrison Wells, yes, I DO think he is someone from the future; he has knowledge of the future.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:04.760
Clearly.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.180
The thing about his wife dying though: that's* truth.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.180
Regardless of where he is from in the timeline --

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.180
like, he came back in time and got stuck

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:14.660
-- I feel like his wife did die in a car crash (or died in an accident).

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.600
So he's telling the truth about his wife.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:19.940
He's just not telling the truth about where he's from and his real identity.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:21.120
For those that are asking: 

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:24.120
Gorilla Grodd will be back in Episode 15, at least.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.340
I don't expect to see him in next week's episode.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:30.200
But because General Eiling is back, we might get a Grodd-Easter egg at the end of the episode.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.720
Hopefully we'll get an Easter Egg for the new Weather Wizard too, because he'll be back in Episode 15.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.340
Or he'll debut* in Episode 15.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.260
So lots of stuff to look forward to.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.540
Lots of time travel.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.860
The "Other" Reverse Flash? 

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:42.020
...finding out who HE is.

00:09:42.177 --> 00:09:43.737
Although I totally think it's Eddie Thawne.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.295
You guys can let me know if you agree though.

00:09:45.295 --> 00:09:47.680
The "Other" Reverse Flash -- who is he?

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:50.020
I didn't really have any big Thumbs Down about the episode.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.680
I thought they had a really interesting choice in music. 

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:53.600
I mean, "Uptown Funk" at the beginning was kinda funny.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.180
Sometimes the songs they pick are a little bit weird and it takes you out of it.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.940
Something else I also noticed:

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:02.520
I feel like Malese Jow is kinda like a 'Felicity'-type character.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.100
Notice what she's wearing. 

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:07.040
She always seems like she's dressed, to catch you're eye.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:12.540
Like everyone else in the background is dressed in really plain colors, but she's wearing this crazy-looking pattern.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:16.660
I tried to find an Easter egg in her dress but I didn't see anything that jumped out at me.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.091
If you think her dress (like that pattern) is an Easter egg for some comic book thing, let me know.

00:10:21.091 --> 00:10:23.611
In related news, I know a lot of you are asking about my Gotham video. 

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:27.560
It's just because of the special video---the fun video I posted yesterday---I had to move it around.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.180
I AM posting Gotham next.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.975
I'll get that out before Arrow tonight.

00:10:30.975 --> 00:10:33.795
I don't know if I'll get my 'Agent Carter' video out before that though.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.120
If I don't, I'll just post it after Arrow on Thursday. So don't worry.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:39.834
I'm also doing Q&amp;A's for The Flash and Arrow this week.

00:10:39.834 --> 00:10:41.914
And for the big Marvel/Sony announcement. 

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.020
So there's plenty of time to ask questions.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:44.900
Think of stuff for that.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:48.680
Okay, so while you guys wait for all that to happen, you can click here* to catch up on The Flash.

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.140
And you can click here* for my Explainer for the Spiderman/Marvel announcement.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.320
"Spiderman in the MCU".

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.820
Everyone is STILL freaking out. 

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.480
I'm still freaking out a little bit about it.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.020
So thank you so much for watching.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.240
Everybody high-five.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:00.540
I'll see you tomorrow.  

